    {
      "title": "Test the product on each interval",
      "body": "<p>Record all three factor signs between consecutive boundaries, then combine them.</p>",
      "recap": "A trigonometric product inequality is solved by ordering its zeros, testing signs and adding accepted interval lengths.",
      "pitfall": "When two factors vanish at the same point, the product need not change sign there.",
      "pause": "Include permitted zeros, exclude poles and calculate the total interval length.",
